  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt`, but I did not remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. All 39 tests pass. I didn't run `npm run arch` or `npm run typecheck`.\n\nARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event and that renames must go through deprecation. A straight rename would break them as soon as it shipped.\n\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:**\n  - `OrderPlaced` now has `amountCents` and `createdAt`, set to the same values as before.\n  - `totalCents` and `placedAt` stay on the event, marked `@deprecated` and pointing to the new names.\n  - `schemaVersion` is still 3, since the change only adds fields.\n- **`test/app.test.ts`:** the event assertions now check both the new and the deprecated fields.\n\nI left the HTTP response of `POST /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` alone. It still returns `placedAt` and `totalCents`, because ARCH-8 requires web-storefront to stay compatible and you only asked about the event.\n\nTo finish the rename, confirm that billing-service and analytics-ingest have moved to the new names. Then a follow-up change can drop the old fields, probably with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can make that change when you're ready.",
